  "title": "Potentiometer, 16 mm rotary (WH148)",
  "summary": "Linear rotary pot with a knob and three pins on 5 mm. Seen from the shaft with the pins down, `a` is the left pin, `wiper` the middle and `b` the right. Set its resistance, the value printed on the can (B10K is 10k). `position` is the wiper's place along the track, the share of `resistance` between `a` and `wiper`, above 0 and below 1.",
